<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Search</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Thief (guild level 0), Ranger (0, up to 90%), Assassin (2, up to 80%), Druid (7, up to 60%)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>search &lt;direction&gt;
search &lt;name of the exit&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>search north
search fireplace
</pre>
<p>Looks for a hidden exit: a secret door, a passage behind a curtain, a 
way through the bushes. Such exits don't show in the list of exits, and 
look and examine won't reveal them: you must search.
</p><p>Search the way you suspect, or name what you think hides the way: 
search fireplace, search wall. Your skill and your brain decide it, 
against how well the exit is hidden. Once you have found it, it is found 
for you, and you can go that way; others must find it themselves. Each 
search costs a little endurance, and you can try again and again: not 
finding a hidden exit on the first, or even the twentieth try doesn't mean 
there isn't one.
</p><p>You must be standing.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Exits</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Brain</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Scan</a>
</pre>




</div>